# APP-SPLIT-003C — gates log (2026-11-26)

Slice of APP-SPLIT-001 (RUN-2 resume recipe): the pack/session/claims
refresh wiring slice extracted from App() into
`apps/desktop/src/app/pack-wiring.ts` as a pure move.

## What moved (verbatim; token-identical bodies, see pure-move check)

- `runRefreshLanguages(deps, pid?)` — the `refreshLanguages` body: the
  four pack reads (installed_packs, pack_claims, loadSessionPack,
  catalog_packs) run together and commit in one block.
- `runRefreshInstalled(deps)` — the `refreshInstalled` body (one read,
  one container update).
- `runUpdateFromCatalog(deps, id)` — the wizard's Update control body.
- `runInstallCatalogPack(deps, packId)` — Settings catalogue install.
- `runCancelInstall(deps)` — cancel the in-flight install.
- `runImportPack(deps, dataB64)` — Settings pack-file import.
- `PackWiringDeps` — the props bundle of render values + setters; App()
  builds `packWiringDeps` once per render and passes it at every call
  site. Built right after `useServeProbe` (earliest point where every
  referenced binding is in scope) so the boot effect's async IIFE, which
  calls `refreshInstalled()` before the first render's tail completes,
  never hits an uninitialized bundle — verified by the restart-resume /
  first-run / pack-install journeys.

App.tsx keeps owning every hook (including `useServeProbe` and all pack
state), the thin wrapper functions, `switchLearning`, the onboarding
`install()`, and all JSX. No test, gate script, or behavior pin was
touched. Test tree swept for `from "./App"` imports: all point at the
primitives re-export shim (App.test.tsx, serve-banner.test.tsx),
untouched by this slice — no re-exports added or removed.

